WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.031
DS-1000 is built through a five-stage pipeline.

00:00:03.111 --> 00:00:06.473
Annotators first select high-vote, testable, useful,

00:00:06.553 --> 00:00:11.172
and representative StackOverflow problems and
rewrite them for clarity.

00:00:11.252 --> 00:00:17.592
They add a code context with insertion markers
showing exactly where the model must fill in code.

00:00:17.672 --> 00:00:23.351
They then implement automatic tests that check
functional correctness by executing test

00:00:23.431 --> 00:00:26.528
cases and also enforce surface-form constraints,

00:00:26.608 --> 00:00:30.698
such as forbidding certain APIs or keywords in the
syntax tree.

00:00:30.778 --> 00:00:35.132
To defend against memorization, they perturb each
original problem,

00:00:35.212 --> 00:00:42.678
using surface perturbations that leave the
reference solution unchanged and semantic perturbations that change it,

00:00:42.758 --> 00:00:45.127
plus deliberately difficult rewrites.

00:00:45.207 --> 00:00:50.620
Finally they red-team the evaluation, requiring it
to reject known-wrong solutions.

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:56.180
Every problem, solution, and metric is reviewed by
at least three expert annotators.
